==Enemy==
On top of having strong Single Attacks and being able to weaken cats, Zroco has a remarkably short burrow duration and distance compared to other Zombies, leaving you with almost no breathing room before it appears right in the middle of your ranged stack. It has the same health as a [[Zoge]], with slightly longer range but only one knockback, so it's dangerous if it resurfaces in the right place at the right time.

==Strategy==
Draw [[Cat Capsule#Rare Capsule|Rare Cat Capsules]] to obtain [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Wushu Cat]], which functions well as both an offensive and defensive counter to Zroco; or stack meatshields, as Zroco is single-target and will take some time chewing through each cat. The use of [[Li'l Bird Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Flying Cat]] or [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver BearCat]] might be necessary to dispose of it in later stages.

Zroco's very short burrow can also be exploited for other purposes. For example, it can surface in a group of meatshields and give [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jellycat]] a chance to fire its [[Wave Attack]], while its revival means the next Jellycat you spawn might be able to exploit this again, as its low range means it's easy to pull off.

